      "value": "@{64dc41752be0c991ddfe9e38|full_name} I have a 5700X3D. But do you know that the main thread of VRChat is single-threaded? That means most of the game rendering is limited to one core. \n\nSecondly, FSR will not help with VRAM usage. If you load a bunch of poorly optimized avatars, they will consume VRAM, and that's just expected.\n\nWhat is your GPU usage with VSync disabled? This is the only factor that actually tells if you are CPU limited or not. If your GPU usage is not maxed out, then FSR will be useless.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
